Exit Angle Table
To open the table of the Exit Angles at which the MUs leave the Turntable, click this button.
Remarks
You can view or fine-tune these settings:
• The number of the Successor.
• The name of the Successor.
• The Angle at which the Connector from the Turntable connects toward this successor.
• At Which Side it turns toward the successor.
◦ If you select Start Point, the Turntable turns with the side, at which you started inserting the
Turntable toward this successor.
◦ If you select End Point, the Turntable turns with the side, at which you finished inserting the
Turntable toward this successor.
◦ If you select Any, the Turntable computes the smallest angle and turns with this computed side
toward this successor. With this setting the MU can leave backward or forward, depending on the side
which can be reached with the smallest angle.
◦ If you select MU keeps Direction, the Turntable turns this side of the Turntable toward this successor
which makes the MU keep its direction.
• If you select MU leaves backward, the Turntable turns this side of the Turntable toward this successor
so that the Turntable turns the MU around, and it leaves moving backward. Compare MU Leaves
Backwards Depends On.
Exit Angle Table
